<title>USA: NYPA 780 MW Fitzpatrick nuke seen on line Thursday.</title>
<headline>NYPA 780 MW Fitzpatrick nuke seen on line Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Power Authority's (NYPA) 780 megawatt James A. Fitzpatrick nuclear power plant in Scriba, N.Y., will likely synchronize to the electricity grid on Thursday, a company spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The twelveth (of December) is still a good working number (for a restart). We are proceeding with the restart testing process,&quot; said company spokesman Carl Patrick.</p>
<p>The unit began startup on Monday from a scheduled maintenance and refueling shutdown Oct 26.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
